sentences.l:
And as when a man gazes at a singer, who from the gods
sings, having learned, words full of longing for mortals,
and of him unceasingly they are eager to hear, whenever he sings;

he declares of Odysseus to have heard,
near, in the rich land of the Thesprotian men,
alive;

But if she comes to know you telling all things unerringly,
she will clothe you in a cloak and a tunic, of which you most
are in need;
